---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Editorial standards"
  description="The sourcing, authorship, disclosure, correction, independence, and AI-assistance standards used by MelodyMind Reviews."
>
  <article class="standards reading-shell">
    <h1>The argument must remain inspectable.</h1>
    <section>
      <h2>Authorship and responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        Daniel Schmid is the named launch author. MelodyMind Editorial defines the
        publication standard and records corrections. A byline identifies who accepts
        responsibility for the final judgment.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Sources and observation</h2>
      <p>
        Release dates, credits, quotations, and historical claims require traceable
        sources. Statements about arrangement, performance, production, and sequence are
        critical observations. They are presented as interpretation, not neutral fact.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="ai-transparency">
      <h2>AI assistance</h2>
      <p>
        Research and drafting may use AI assistance. Sources are checked separately,
        generated claims without support are removed, and every published article carries
        a disclosure. AI assistance does not receive a byline and does not erase human
        editorial responsibility.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Independence and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Reviews are not paid placements and do not use affiliate links. MelodyMind’s own
        music is excluded from independent review coverage. Material corrections add an
        updated date and a plain account of what changed.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .standards {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-block: var(--space-4xl);
  }

  .standards h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }

  .standards section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-xl);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .standards section h2 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
  }

  .standards section p {
    color: var(--quiet-ink);
  }
</style>
